WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.461
Not every value made of digits should be stored as a
number Identifiers are a

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:11.158
good example An employee ID ZIP code account code or
diagnosis code

00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:17.194
may contain digits but we normally do not add or
average those values Keeping

00:00:17.221 --> 00:00:22.855
an identifier as text also protects important
formatting An ID such as zero

00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:27.960
zero one two five has leading zeros If we treat it
as a numeric quantity

00:00:28.131 --> 00:00:33.635
those leading zeros may be lost When choosing a data
type ask

00:00:33.661 --> 00:00:38.467
what the value means not only what it looks like If
it represents a label

00:00:38.493 --> 00:00:41.664
rather than a quantity a string is often the better
choice
